  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\nThe traced playback worker now cuts the whole program one time when the transport starts. It keeps keyframes of the cut stock at a fixed stride. After that, a jump forward or back restores the keyframe at or before the playhead and cuts at most one stride. The program is not cut again during playback.\r\n\r\n- `crates/sim/src/play_keys.rs`: `Precalc` state and the checkpoint store, with byte accounting and thinning shared by precalculation and live seeks after cancellation (512 MiB default budget, at most 1024 keyframes, at least 64 moves apart initially).\r\n- `crates/sim/src/play_precalc.rs`: begin/step orchestration, checkpoint policy and the calculation loop through the `Playback` seam. `Keyframes::restores` is the one seek law for `FieldPlay::seek` and the worker.\r\n- `crates/sim/src/play_precalc_mailbox.rs`: progress and cancellation state, with caller-provided stop and elapsed-time bindings.\r\n- `crates/app/src/stock_play_precalc.rs`, `stock_play_worker_precalc.rs`: thin adapters for the existing `FieldPlay` and `PlayWorker` APIs. App retains document gathering, thread lifetime, wakeups, clock binding and frame publication. It re-exports the sim API where needed.\r\n- `crates/app/src/stock_play.rs`, `stock_play_worker.rs`: a seek restores a keyframe that is more than one stride ahead, not only one behind. A `moves_cut` counter measures the replay law.\r\n- `crates/ui/src/actions.rs`: the transport starts the worker with the calculation.\r\n- `crates/ui/src/play_precalc.rs` (new), `egui_app/shell.rs`: a line under the transport shows the progress and a Cancel button. A stopped calculation shows \"incomplete\" with the reason.\r\n- `docs/decisions/2181-sim-precalc.md`: the design and the dropped options.\r\n\r\nThe stamp is `doc_version`. Each command retires the worker and frees its keyframes (an operation delete included). The keyframes are display only. The Deviate verdict and the post gate do not read them.\r\n\r\n## Readings\r\n\r\nRelease, dense face (100 mm block, stepover 0.5, stepdown 0.5, `DEFAULT_TEXELS`), `precalc_reading_on_the_dense_face`:\r\n\r\n- 4268 moves, 68 keyframes, stride 64\r\n- keyframe memory 444940288 bytes (424 MiB, under the 512 MiB budget)\r\n- calculation time 23.9 s\r\n\r\nDuring the calculation the sheet stands and the line shows the progress. Follow-up #2193 serves frames during the calculation. Follow-up #2194 lowers the keyframe memory.\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n`crates/app/tests/stock_play_precalc.rs`:\r\n- `the_precalculated_stock_is_the_live_cut_at_every_position` (bit-identical cut layer at each move, forward and back jumps mixed)\r\n- `a_jump_after_the_calculation_cuts_at_most_one_stride` (no new full calculation)\r\n- `the_keyframes_stay_within_the_memory_budget`\r\n- `a_stopped_calculation_leaves_exact_keyframes_and_cuts_the_rest_live`\r\n- `the_worker_calculates_first_then_replays_and_the_post_gate_is_unchanged` (`posting::verification_gate` is equal before and after)\r\n- `a_cancelled_calculation_is_incomplete_by_name_and_playback_goes_on`\r\n- `precalc_reading_on_the_dense_face` (ignored, heavy lane, the reading above)\r\n\r\n`crates/sim/tests/play_precalc.rs` (#2192 review, finding 4):\r\n- `domain_calculation_resets_cuts_and_reports_the_bounded_store`\r\n- `domain_mailbox_cancel_preserves_partial_checkpoints_and_names_the_end`\r\n- `domain_mailbox_reports_progress_and_uses_the_owners_stop_and_clock`\r\n- `a_seek_restores_behind_or_more_than_a_stride_ahead`\r\n\r\n`crates/ui/src/play_precalc_tests.rs`:\r\n- `the_readout_says_progress_and_incomplete_and_nothing_when_done`\r\n- `an_edit_of_the_operation_retires_the_stored_calculation`\r\n\r\n## Gate\r\n\r\nFix round at head 5d929ae (finding 4 again; the local commit 738492b of the earlier round was never pushed, so this round makes the move again on the pushed branch):\r\n\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-sim --test play_precalc --test play_keys`: 4 + 4 pass.\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test stock_play --test stock_play_precalc --test stock_play_partial --test stock_sim_document`: 7, 7 (1 ignored, the heavy reading), 3, 9 pass.\r\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib precalc`: 6 pass (the transport row and readout tests). No ui file changed in this round.\r\n- Clippy with `-D warnings`: sim all targets; app lib and the four suites above; ui lib and tests.\r\n- Mutation: with the keyframe offer removed from `play_precalc::step`, two of the new sim pins fail. The restored source passes.\r\n- Not run: the quick tier (over one hour on sim branches), the full app and ui suites, the heavy lanes.\r\n\r\n## Screenshots\r\n\r\nHeadless render of the real shell (test harness, 1280x720), captured in the earlier fix round and preserved from image commit `a94079e073ac7e38f14569eca085dec7a903e17a`. The before image shows the transport before precalculation. The after images show the reviewed transport change. These PNGs are hosted only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\r\n\r\nBefore: the transport row has no precalculation line.\r\n\r\n![before](<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-2192/before-transport.png>)\r\n\r\nAfter, while the calculation runs: the progress text and the Cancel button.\r\n\r\n![after running](<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-2192/after-running.png>)\r\n\r\nAfter, when Cancel stopped the calculation: the \"incomplete\" text with the reason. There is no Cancel button.\r\n\r\n![after incomplete](<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-2192/after-incomplete.png>)\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The windowed app was not started. The screenshots come from the headless test harness render of the real shell.\r\n- The reading uses one large fixture only.\r\n\r\n## Overlap\r\n\r\n#2182 changes other hunks of `crates/ui/src/actions.rs` (status strings). The two PRs do not stack.\r\n\r\nChangelog: Simulation playback calculates the stock removal one time before it plays, then replays it, so a jump on the timeline does not lag. A line under the transport shows the progress and can cancel the calculation.\r\n\r\nEffort: high (issue label effort:max; an Opus worker of the high tier works it by the maintainer's order; no escalation)\r\n\r\nFixes #2181\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
